# Family A6: envelope/payload pooling (internal/pool). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/pool
BENCH=BenchmarkPool
REF=none
AUTO_KEY=pool
ADR=14
TITLE="Envelope and payload pooling (A6)"
# The end-to-end view (BenchmarkMemory/PubSubAck pool= dimension, gc-cycles/op,
# max-rss-MB) is measured by the engine's bake-off once A12 lands.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="throughput + GC pause; adopt only if measurably better -> free list for reuse mode"
# MATRIX=full, narrowed. The two dimensions that move either half of the
# criterion are the goroutine count -- a per-P cache (sync.Pool) and a shared
# free list part company under contention and nowhere else -- and the buffer
# size, where §10.4's payload ladder reaches 64 KiB and a pool stops competing
# with the allocator and starts competing with the collector. The smoke grid
# has neither (P=1,4 and 64 B/1 KiB), so `full` now sweeps P{1,8,32} and every
# size §10.4 names and drops the in-flight-depth cross, which no criterion
# reads: 12 rows per kind rather than 20, 60 for the family (assumption
# A24.61).
MATRIX=full
DECIDED_AT="GetPut Buffers P=1 P=32 size=64 size=65536"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op gc-cycles/op max-rss-MB"
# GC *pause* is not reported by any row: BenchmarkPool reports gc-cycles/op
# and max-rss-MB, which is the cycle count and the footprint, not the pause
# distribution §10.3.4 asks for. §9.1's end-to-end
# `BenchmarkMemory/PubSubAck/{safe,owned,reuse}/<pool>` cross and its GOGC
# sweep are also unmeasured; assumption A24.9 already records that the cross is
# left to the increment that owns A6, and A24.68 records the pause metric.
# (A CRITERION_GAP value is prose and its entries are separated by ";", so
# the reason cannot itself contain one.)
CRITERION_GAP="gc-pause-ns=unmeasured. No arm in this tree samples runtime/metrics GC pause quantiles, and what BenchmarkPool reports instead is gc-cycles/op and max-rss-MB (assumption A24.68)"
